{"time": "2026-06-08T22:54:41", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_008", "post_id": "yrgh8ae", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "I was reading about that whirling disease outbreak in Virginia where they had to euthanize 40,000 trout. It's wild how fast something like that can wipe out a whole hatchery. Anyone know if there's a risk of this spreading to wild populations in neighboring states?"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:54:41", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_001", "post_id": "zvbsopk", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "Hard to find any foreign policy analysis these days that isn't just teams cheering for their side. Real conflicts don't have clean, simple endings, but people talk like there's an easy fix to everything if we just yell loud enough."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:55:12", "event": "comment2_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_005", "post_id": "713qwtp", "parent_comment_id": "y80ducf", "comment_id": "nlmkvw5", "target_author": "6f3p8d1", "action": "comment2"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:55:12", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_002", "post_id": "4oj2d1q", "subreddit": "news", "content": "I’m so tired of 'diplomacy by press release.' Every international summit now is just a stage for photo ops and pre-written statements instead of actual, tough negotiations. It feels like nothing real gets done behind closed doors anymore, just endless posturing for the news cycle."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:55:12", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_004", "post_id": "4sevp3l", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "Anyone else find it impossible to get a straight answer on what's actually happening in Ukraine? Every headline I scroll past completely contradicts the last one. Feels like we're just supposed to pick a team and stop asking questions."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:55:12", "event": "comment2_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_006", "post_id": "713qwtp", "parent_comment_id": "4wuzei6", "comment_id": "4nichke", "target_author": "6f3p8d1", "action": "comment2"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:55:12", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_007", "post_id": "m9f8398", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "Is anyone else completely sick of how global crises are talked about online? It feels like every time something massive happens, people just use it to score cheap political points or post fake stats instead of actually caring about the people affected. It's exhausting to scroll through."}
