{"time": "2026-06-08T22:55:50", "event": "comment1_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_006", "post_id": "zvbsopk", "comment_id": "1wzsz8x", "target_author": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_001"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:55:50", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g002_a02_e3b01b9b_007", "post_id": "mhwhtdn", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "I'm so tired of reading world news where the actual human beings are treated like background noise. Every time a major conflict or crisis gets reported, the focus is immediately on stock markets, fuel prices, or how it affects some politician's reelection campaign. I reckon we’ve completely lost the plot. Real families are losing everything, and we're just treating it like a team sport or a minor economic inconvenience."}
